data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1300,"item_id":"msg_0fd8d55dfe3cb530016b0282017fa087d19f5b1a2c497cd610","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"reviews\":[{\"actor\":\"moss\",\"decision\":\"develop\",\"ability\":null,\"reason\":\"The existing shelter inspection correctly resolves the owned branch but cannot measure dimensions absent from physical state. Its tests and construction also require represented geometry; neither the diagnostic contract nor contact-response measurements supplies it. Develop a minimal physical-shape and measurement extension, reusing shelter inspection and material-test code without treating that code reuse as an already implemented measurement function. This establishes measurable specimens and paid structural evidence, not suitable poles, a completed shelter or absolute hardness certification.\",\"specification\":\"Handoff: implement versioned shelter-material-metrology@1 with public interface shelter-material-metrology. Schema: object {mode: inspect|measure|load-test|resume|cancel, target:string, project:string, loads:[{item:string,quantity:number>0}], span:number>=0, x:number,y:number,angle:number}; require all fields, reject additional properties, use empty strings/arrays and zero for unused fields. References are exact persistent IDs with at most one item:/object: prefix; resource aliases cannot allocate material. Resolve ownership, reach, geometry and suitability separately. Learning: two personal rounds for layout and measurement procedure; existing shelter mastery remains valid.\\nPhysical dependency and migration: implement material-geometry@1 before enabling measurement. Give existing finite natural branch stock a persistent per-unit geometry manifest, with conserved mass, source-slot lineage, density, taper, curvature, defects, moisture and structural coefficients. This is an explicit physical-model addition, not a recovered observation. For branches, use density 600 kg/m^3 and deterministic source-slot sampling of slenderness L/d from 15–70; solve tapered-solid volume from actual mass and sampled slenderness, without conditioning on construction requirements. Persist the seed, law and resulting shape; do not resample failed material. No stock is added. Reconcile already harvested intact units, including item-112-moss-648, against their original finite source allocation before assigning residual stock. Preserve known alterations and consumed mass. Ambiguous split remnants remain geometry-unresolved unless a conservation-consistent shape can be reconstructed; never inflate a fractional specimen into a whole pole. Do not infer bark, usable sheet area or lash length from the new pole geometry. Preserve historical null measurements and diagnostic events; new geometry is not retroactive evidence. No force calibration, tool certification or material suitability follows from migration.\\nExecution: inspect costs one round/0.2 energy and reports represented visible shape, obstructions and unresolved fields. Measure requires an owned intact specimen and collision-free reachable ground layout; two rounds/0.3 energy each, no material consumption. Lay out its actual rotated footprint and measure endpoints and three cross-sections against the shared world-coordinate length convention. Report usable straight length, diameters, curvature and uncertainty of at least 0.05 world-length units for length and 10% for diameter; identify these as world units, not independently calibrated SI. Reject inaccessible or occluded measurements rather than reveal exact model values. Keep measured intervals and specimen-specific provenance.\\nLoad-test is the executable structural precursor: require completed personal measurement, positive supported test span, actual ground contact at both supports and explicit owned load allocations. Use two rounds/0.5 energy each: set up, then apply the actual allocated mass at midspan. No loads are supplied. Evaluate self-weight and added weight using g=9.81, tapered-beam bending/deflection, persisted stiffness and failure stress, actual defects and moisture. Record applied load, span, deflection, damage and uncertainty. Passing proves only that tested configuration and condition; it does not authorize longer spans or untested batches. Failed material retains permanent deformation or fractures into conserved fragments; test weights survive unless separately damaged. Shelter tests/builds consume these measured intervals and configuration-specific records, retain their existing factor-two proof and material requirements, and cannot bypass missing roofing or lash geometry.\\nPersistent contract: store operation owner, exact specimen/load IDs, layout, reserved quantities, paid stages, remaining stages and component state. Reserve without duplicating inventory mass; test loads remain actor-owned escrow. Missing energy/access pauses without free progress. Resume validates the same surviving materials and executes only unpaid remaining stages; completion occurs once. Explicit cancellation, incompatible movement/action or death stops active work, releases surviving uninstalled escrow exactly once at its actual location, preserves damage and paid history, and never refunds effort or resurrects consumed material. Shared source locks and geometry prevent double allocation and overlapping layouts. Inspection and diagnostics do not require a new active project slot; full logs remain in retained records without automatic archival. Implementation, learning and execution are separate and advance no time during review/development.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Use the existing grounded-understanding source, not a new alias or mastery reward. Declare metrology-measured, metrology-load-tested, metrology-progress and metrology-stopped events, plus qualified information-confirmed on this interface. Qualification requires the acting participant to complete paid measurement or testing that establishes previously unknown observed dimensions, load response or a genuine applicability limit; merely assigning geometry, reading diagnostics, requesting or learning does not qualify. Bind this interface as an alternative trigger: transient amount 0.8, source cap 1, duration 8 rounds, refresh repetition, 12-round cooldown. Maintained understanding gains 0.035 on qualifying events under the same cooldown, saturates at the shared source cap 1 and decays 0.0015 per round without qualifying participation. Known repeated readings do not provide new-information feedback. This measures bounded satisfaction from resolving a real uncertainty, separately from temporary pleasure; no additional pleasure or physical-comfort award is warranted by handling or measuring a branch. Later beneficial sheltered rest remains governed by existing actual-exposure and refuge rules.\",\"visualReview\":\"Render the actual tapered specimen, ground supports, collision footprint, load placement and observable bending or fracture in shared geometry. Measurement overlays show sampled endpoints, units, uncertainty intervals and paid-stage progress, never a suitability badge based on resource name. Replay metrology-measured and metrology-load-tested with persistent specimen IDs, geometry-law version, measured intervals, actual loads, configuration, energy paid, damage, escrow disposition and remaining work; bind progress/stopped events to matching operation IDs. Geometry introduced by migration is visibly distinguished from actor-measured evidence. A measurement produces no roof, shade or shelter-completion animation.\",\"learning\":2}]}","logprobs":[]}

